joshua_russo: .....
player: .....?
joshua_russo: ......
player: Russo? [pause=0.5]What are you staring at?
joshua_russo: Oh, Boss, don’t mind me. [pause=0.5]Well, guess our victim wanted to play God. [pause=0.5]Not the weirdest thing we’ve found in a victim’s belongings. [pause=0.5]Heh. [pause=0.5]Here’s hoping THOSE memories don’t come back to you.
player: Does this person look like anyone connected to the case?
joshua_russo: Hmm… not that I could say. [pause=0.5]I’ll let you know if I spot anyone missing half a head.[pause=0.5]\
\
Jokes aside, I’m not thinking this is anything important. [pause=0.5]I’ll just go ahead and stick this in my pocket.
Russo moves to grab it, but you pull it closer to your face.
player: ....Wait.
joshua_russo: Huh?
player: Given the ink on this, the picture was burned AFTER someone wrote on it and scribbled out this face.
joshua_russo: ...I guess you’re right. [pause=0.5]What difference does it make?
player: Why would they stop burning it halfway if it was someone they would scribble the face out for?
joshua_russo: Not sure, Boss. Maybe they just regretted it halfway through.[pause=0.5] Not like all of this had to have happened in one night. Might’ve been their only picture of this person.
player: Perhaps.[pause=0.5] …Wait, I just realized, how did the victim die anyways? [pause=0.5]I’ll need all the details if I’m going to do anything productive.
joshua_russo: Oh, yeah. [pause=0.5]Suppose I could tell you. [pause=0.5]Struck over the head with something, what it is, we’re not sure. [pause=0.5]It was pretty brutal though, they–
player: *hurp* [pause=1]Stop! Stop! Stop!
joshua_russo: Boss?
player: I, uh…[pause=1]never mind. [pause=0.5]Tell me later.
joshua_russo: Got it, don’t need anything like that in your jumbled mind right now. [pause=0.5]Hey, hey. [pause=0.5]Take it easy. [pause=0.5]Anything I can do for you, you let me know.
player: Thanks, Russo.
joshua_russo: Any time.